Package: winstepsR
Title: Generate Input Files for 'Winsteps', Run It, and Read the Output
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Anthony", "Raborn", email = "anthony@raborndecisionsciences.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A thin, organization-agnostic interface between R and the Rasch
    measurement program 'Winsteps' (<https://www.winsteps.com/index.htm>).
    Given item response data in long format and a set of anchored item
    difficulties, it writes the 'Winsteps' person-response data file, item
    anchor file, and control file; runs 'Winsteps' in batch mode; and reads
    the resulting person output file (PFILE) back into R as a tibble. It
    intentionally does not implement any exam-specific scoring rules
    (scale-score conversions, penalty rules, domain definitions, and the
    like) -- those belong in the calling project, not in this package.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/AnthonyRaborn/winstepsR
BugReports: https://github.com/AnthonyRaborn/winstepsR/issues
SystemRequirements: Winsteps (<https://www.winsteps.com/index.htm>), which is
    licensed separately and runs on Windows only. Generating input files and
    reading output works on any platform; winsteps_run() does not.
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    stats,
    tidyr,
    readr,
    tibble,
    utils
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
